PLAIN-1434	iron since the human body has no mechanism to excrete excess iron , it is probably best to refrain from consuming blood-based ( heme ) iron and taking iron supplements unless prescribed ( for example , for pregnant women who are demonstrably anemic ) . this is because iron pills have been linked to birth complications such as preterm birth and maternal hypertension . presumably because of iron ’ s pro-oxidant qualities , it can be a double-edged sword ; lowering the iron level of cancer patients has been associated with dropping death rates . the absorption of plant-based ( non-heme ) iron can be regulated by the body , though , making dark green leafy veggies and legumes such as lentils preferable sources , especially since food is a package deal . - plant-based diets , meat , animal products , vegetarians , vegans , vegetables , beans , chicken , mortality , beef , standard american diet , nuts , poultry , turkey , pork - -
